WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:17.600
Oh my God!

2
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.640
Calm down!
Good morning, sweetie.

3
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Calm down.

4
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.080
What's going on?
- Careful.

5
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.120
There's a tiny human
growing inside of you.

6
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:33.240
We don't want to scare it
so early in the morning, right?

7
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.640
Softly. Here.

8
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.360
Here you go.
- I'm not hungry.

9
00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.640
The baby wants to eat. Here.

10
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:43.240
Softly. Have a bite.

11
00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.560
Great.

12
00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:48.960
Here...

13
00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:52.240
Have a drink.

14
00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.080
Calm, calm. Don't rush.

15
00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.240
Don't spill it.

16
00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:00.560
Get up now.

17
00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.080
Don't get crumbs everywhere.

18
00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:15.280
Eat up!

19
00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:19.160
Listen up now.

20
00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:22.080
You're going to stay calm.

21
00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:23.880
As calm as I am.

22
00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:27.480
Drink, drink, drink.

23
00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:32.600
I'll listen.

24
00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:37.400
It's eating!

25
00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:40.160
It's munching.

26
00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:43.880
Come on, eat!

27
00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:47.280
DIVORCE IN PEACE

28
00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:50.480
I needed to finish
my school project somehow.

29
00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:53.800
Something visual
and related to new media.

30
00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:56.520
Something that had something.

31
00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:58.800
That's how I came up with the idea.

32
00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:02.400
This is a school project, right?

33
00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:04.840
And now it's online?

34
00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:06.280
Well, alright then.

35
00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:09.240
Nowadays, everything's online.
- Wait a minute.

36
00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:11.400
I mean, who'd even watch us?

37
00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.280
You'll remove it after the exam.

38
00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:18.320
Yeah, that's true. I mean,
if there are only a few viewers.

39
00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.080
That's the problem.
There are more than a few viewers.

40
00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.400
Oh my God,
do I really look like that?

41
00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.960
Hold on!
Is this the number of viewers?

42
00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.960
That's the number of viewers.
- 2000 viewers!?

43
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.920
Two million.

44
00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:38.720
Million?

45
00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:41.800
They're fans.

46
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.480
Most are foreigners.
Japanese and French.

47
00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:48.320
From Tartu, too.
- Why do they care about our life?

48
00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.360
Japanese people are
watching us getting a divorce?

49
00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:52.760
They're rooting for you.

50
00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:54.640
Some are rooting for you.

51
00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:56.640
Some are rooting for dad.

52
00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:59.080
'Is this man real?'

53
00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:01.280
God...

54
00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:05.000
'I'd shoot myself if I were Aksel.'

55
00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.960
The women are mainly rooting for me.

56
00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:11.880
Looks like men, too.

57
00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:15.520
'Laura, will you marry me?'
- Where?

58
00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:17.800
We're your exam submission.

59
00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:23.960
Our boy secretly filmed us
and uploaded it on YouTube,

60
00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:25.680
and now the entire world is laughing.

61
00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.560
But we are ridiculous.

62
00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.360
You don't do these kinds of things!

63
00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:33.440
Secretly filming us?
This is a private matter!

64
00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:35.360
You're abusing our trust.

65
00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.640
You film us in secret,
don't say a single word,

66
00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:41.320
and now that there are two million
viewers, you decide to say something?

67
00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:42.400
Let him be.

68
00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:45.160
That journalist wants to talk to you.
- What!?

69
00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:48.120
I'm not doing any interview.
They can kiss my ass!

70
00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.920
You have that right.

71
00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:52.480
You're also not doing it.
- Says who?

72
00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:55.120
You want to join in on this joke?

73
00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:58.800
Are you some kind of influencer now?

74
00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:01.040
Maybe Mihkel will benefit from it?

75
00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:02.560
Take it down!

76
00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:05.560
What will I show my exam
committee then? A screen shot?

77
00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:08.680
Show them a wiener for all I care!

78
00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:11.120
But we are not your guinea pigs!

79
00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.600
I'll talk to dad.

80
00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:19.840
Yes?

81
00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:21.800
Oh my God,
a buyer is coming.

82
00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:23.360
Stay calm and be polite.

83
00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:25.960
Our personal drama will
not drive down the house price!

84
00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:27.280
Yes, of course.

85
00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:32.200
So, you've set each other free.

86
00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.680
You've come to terms and calmed down.

87
00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:37.240
Now it's time to look.

88
00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:39.680
It's time to face the truth

89
00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:43.240
and admit that all of this is a scam.

90
00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:45.600
It's pointless crap.

91
00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:48.880
It's aimed at gullible people

92
00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:51.360
who are more than happy
to open their wallets for you.

93
00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:52.960
Why do you care?
I'm paying.

94
00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:56.480
I just want to say that
I don't believe in these things.

95
00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:00.720
I don't believe in meditation
or this kind of therapy.

96
00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:03.080
I believe...
- You don't believe in anything.

97
00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:05.760
Things are always tipping
to one side or another for you.

98
00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:07.000
But they are!

99
00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.480
They are tipping.

100
00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:13.120
I'm leaving now.
I don't want to listen to this.

101
00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:14.960
What I want to say

102
00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:17.960
is that I want to believe
that there are things in this world

103
00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:20.160
that are worth believing in.

104
00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:23.120
That two people meet
and find each other...

105
00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:26.400
And then forget about each other.
Is that worth believing?

106
00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:29.400
You're interrupting me.
Please don't.

107
00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:30.760
You're twisting my words.

108
00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:33.320
It's because you
don't know what to say either.

109
00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:36.720
You're just upset that you've been
woken up from your hibernation.

110
00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:39.760
Now you can't lie in your mausoleum,
you have to actually live.

111
00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:41.360
I want to say...

112
00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.120
Just sit and listen!

113
00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:46.240
Sorry.
I'm very sorry about this.

114
00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.480
Don't worry, everything's fine.

115
00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:52.360
So...

116
00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:56.480
The ninth therapy task is...

117
00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:00.000
'Greetings from the future.'

118
00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:02.640
Wow, now we're
heading off into the future?

119
00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:07.760
Esoterically, modernly,
meditatively, spiritually.

120
00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.840
You'll imagine the life you'll have

121
00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:14.480
in ten years' time
without each other.

122
00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:17.200
Then, you'll share that vision
with each other.

123
00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:21.200
You've been separated for ten years,
both living new lives.

124
00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:23.040
You'll close your eyes.

125
00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:25.040
Meditate.

126
00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:27.960
Then, share the vision you see.

127
00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:30.840
Yeah, meditate ourselves flat.

128
00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:33.760
Greetings from the future.

129
00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:37.400
This is the living room.

130
00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:39.520
This is like a cosy cave,

131
00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:41.320
the heart of the house.

132
00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:43.520
It's a great place to hang out

133
00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:45.640
with your kids or another person.

134
00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:51.920
This is it, then.

135
00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:56.040
Hello.

136
00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:57.360
Hello.

137
00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:59.080
You can have a
look at the kitchen.

138
00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:01.920
It has modern solutions
and is very cosy, as well.

139
00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:04.360
Heavy metal, I went for a shit.

140
00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:06.520
Do we have to move out now?

141
00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:10.160
No, we still have a month.
I told you, don't worry.

142
00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:11.960
I'm not worried.
What about the bakery?

143
00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:14.160
The deal with Rihard
is still pending.

144
00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.280
You'll get half, don't worry.

145
00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:18.160
What do I have to worry about?

146
00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:21.800
I don't have a job,
money or a place to live.

147
00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:25.440
I've been publicly
embarrassed on YouTube.

148
00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:27.800
A wonderful way to
start my life under a bush.

149
00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:29.920
Don't forget
you're going to be a dad too.

150
00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:31.440
Right, that as well.

151
00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:34.000
Please call me
'honey' in front of the buyer.

152
00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:37.240
It'll create a cosier atmosphere
and help sell the house.

153
00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:38.280
Yes, honey.

154
00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:41.240
Let's have a look upstairs.
The bathroom's there.

155
00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:43.240
It has family friendly solutions.

156
00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:46.840
The needs of families with small kids
have been taken into account, too.

157
00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:48.320
Let's have a look.

158
00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:52.160
Yes, Tauno?

159
00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:54.880
Yes, I can come.

160
00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:56.520
I'll pop by right now.

161
00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:59.080
Honey.
- Yes, honey?

162
00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:01.320
I'm going to pop by the neighbours'.

163
00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:05.560
To discuss my paternity issue
with Tauno and Mirjam.

164
00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:07.640
Mirjam, our neighbour,

165
00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:11.040
who I knocked up during
our divorce therapy task.

166
00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:12.720
Is that alright?

167
00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:15.120
Buyer, can you hear me?
- Yes?

168
00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:17.560
You see that door
straight in front of the stairs?

169
00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:19.560
That room has an interesting aura.

170
00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:23.680
In spring, a ferret managed to get
inside through the window frame

171
00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:25.440
and pissed all over the carpet.

172
00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:28.560
It smells horrible.
Go and have a whiff yourself.

173
00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:30.040
Yes, honey?

174
00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:35.440
In short,
we don't want anything from you.

175
00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:38.120
You don't have to buy
any diapers for the baby.

176
00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:42.680
You don't have to support Mirjam
or any of that jazz.

177
00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:44.000
And you...

178
00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:47.240
...won't want anything from us.
- Okay.

179
00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:50.440
You're not allowed to
tell the kid that you're the dad.

180
00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:54.040
You're not allowed to
even introduce yourself.

181
00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:55.600
I mean as the dad.

182
00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:57.560
Because you're not the dad.

183
00:08:57.840 --> 00:08:59.480
You just gave...

184
00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:01.320
...the seed.

185
00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:04.080
Yeah.

186
00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:06.320
To confirm things...

187
00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:11.280
We've prepared this.

188
00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:15.360
Do I have to sign this?
- Yes.

189
00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:17.520
A nondisclosure agreement.

190
00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:19.840
Okay, but...

191
00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:22.320
Are you sure this is needed?

192
00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:26.960
For things to be completely clear...

193
00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:28.440
How much do you want?

194
00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:29.720
For what?

195
00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:30.920
For being the donor.

196
00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:34.640
Are you being serious?

197
00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:42.200
Otherwise, it's all over the place.
If it was a present,

198
00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:43.680
then it's incomprehensible.

199
00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:46.880
But if there's payment
and a contract,

200
00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:48.480
then everything's clear.

201
00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:50.440
I don't know.
Are you sure about this?

202
00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:52.520
Accept the help, my friend.

203
00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:55.800
You don't have a job
and you have to move out.

204
00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:58.400
You did a good deed for us.

205
00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:01.120
Let us help you now.

206
00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:06.720
I didn't think about money when I...

207
00:10:07.720 --> 00:10:09.960
When Mirjam and I
were on the couch...

208
00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.080
When Mirjam and...

209
00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:16.680
When Mirjam needed help,
I didn't think about money.

210
00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:21.360
Tauno, it will feel like
I've sold myself to you.

211
00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:24.600
You're crazy, man.

212
00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:28.640
You don't have to
feel like a prostitute.

213
00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:31.360
It's a donor's fee.

214
00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:32.520
Sperm salary.

215
00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:34.760
I don't know...

216
00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:37.640
What's the usual rate for sperm?

217
00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:39.480
Usually 50 euros.

218
00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:40.920
50 euros?

219
00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:42.960
50 for a blast.

220
00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:48.360
I can pay you more
since you're a friend.

221
00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:54.840
I thought...

222
00:10:56.560 --> 00:10:57.880
Let's do...

223
00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:00.920
Let's make it a hundred.

224
00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:04.640
So...

225
00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:06.720
If you don't...

226
00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:09.200
Shit, I only have 500-euro bills.

227
00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:11.760
I'll pay you tomorrow.
Remind me.

228
00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:13.160
Let's have a baby party.

229
00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:14.800
Have a barbeque and sauna.

230
00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:17.000
Make it 150° C.

231
00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:18.640
Alright? So, read it.

232
00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:22.000
Have a look and sign it.

233
00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:26.840
A lot of jam fits there.
It's all been tried and tested.

234
00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:29.960
Apples handle the winter well.
It's a good pantry.

235
00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:32.200
Ave?

236
00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:34.480
You were supposed to be on the train.

237
00:11:37.160 --> 00:11:39.400
What happened, Ave?

238
00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:41.120
Ülo's in the hospital.

239
00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:43.120
Oh my God.

240
00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:45.040
What happened?

241
00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:46.960
He collapsed at the train station.

242
00:11:47.800 --> 00:11:49.320
The ambulance came.

243
00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:53.040
How is he?
What happened?

244
00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:58.080
He just...

245
00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:03.240
He was just depriving
himself eating vegan food.

246
00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:07.320
He had a heart attack because of it.

247
00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:09.160
God.

248
00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:11.720
But he is 21 years older than you.

249
00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:15.160
Just the stress at home
with his wife and kids...

250
00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:17.320
It was too much for him.

251
00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:19.880
What now?

252
00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:21.800
He's in recovery.

253
00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:26.960
Just this entire protest...

254
00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:29.520
Everything's cancelled.

255
00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:31.040
Why?

256
00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:33.720
Ülo's wife is with
him at the hospital.

257
00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:38.280
Ülo's going back home.
- Sweetheart...

258
00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:43.640
It doesn't matter.

259
00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:49.440
I have to find a younger lover.
You two were right.

260
00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:52.280
You were right about everything.

261
00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:04.680
So...

262
00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:08.080
Should we go and
take a look at the garage?

263
00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:19.760
Quality TV.

264
00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:28.560
They took the confession
quite positively.

265
00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:31.440
I think they don't know
what the internet is.

266
00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:33.920
Congratulations.

267
00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:36.920
I have no idea
what I'm going to do with my life.

268
00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:41.800
Everything is so grey without Ülo...

269
00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:44.960
What? Shut up!

270
00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:46.920
It was horrible.

271
00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:50.600
He started foaming at the mouth
and he was calling for his wife.

272
00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:52.040
Really.

273
00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:54.840
That's pretty gross.
- Yeah.

274
00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:58.680
Good that it happened at
the train station, not in Klaipėda.

275
00:13:59.720 --> 00:14:01.160
Thanks...

276
00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:03.360
I feel so much better.

277
00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:06.760
Come on.

278
00:14:07.840 --> 00:14:10.520
Stay happy, stay positive.

279
00:14:13.640 --> 00:14:15.360
You're out of it, Mihkel.

280
00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:20.720
Honestly, it feels better.

281
00:14:21.640 --> 00:14:23.800
Alma does look like mom.

282
00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:26.320
Told you.

283
00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:31.440
Tauno.

284
00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:41.760
Wow, I thought...

285
00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:44.840
Our bedroom would be
a good place for the nursery.

286
00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:47.760
I can sleep in a hammock.

287
00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:50.880
As long as the baby is good. Right?

288
00:14:52.920 --> 00:14:54.480
Is everything alright?

289
00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:57.160
Of course it is.
I was just thinking...

290
00:14:57.760 --> 00:14:59.040
...that this is our time.

291
00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:02.560
We've been running around so much
and doing things.

292
00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:05.160
Is everything okay?
Are you tired?

293
00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:06.800
You look kind of weird.

294
00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:09.920
What do you mean weird?
Is my make-up okay?

295
00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:11.440
No, it's not.

296
00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:13.120
You're weird!

297
00:15:13.160 --> 00:15:14.680
No, I'm just thinking.

298
00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:18.720
My head is full of thoughts.
About the baby.

299
00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:20.960
We have time with that.

300
00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:23.200
Come on, Tauno...

301
00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:24.720
No, we...

302
00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:26.520
No-no, wait now.

303
00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:28.840
We have to take it easy now.

304
00:15:28.880 --> 00:15:34.440
We shouldn't upset
or mess with our little one.

305
00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:38.240
We have to put our wishes aside.

306
00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:42.960
Music, cocktails, everything.
All for the baby.

307
00:15:43.360 --> 00:15:45.360
Yeah, all for the baby.

308
00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:47.720
Take it easy.

309
00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:50.600
So, what do you think
about the bedroom?

310
00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:54.840
So, this is a meditation task.

311
00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:57.040
You have to focus

312
00:15:57.040 --> 00:16:00.200
for the right vision to come to you.

313
00:16:00.280 --> 00:16:03.200
For it to be a proper mess.

314
00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:05.120
Do you want to go first?

315
00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:08.040
Alright.

316
00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:12.560
Just focus and relax,
otherwise the vision won't be right.

317
00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:16.160
I'll try to focus now.

318
00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:20.560
Me in ten years' time.

319
00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:25.000
How old will I be?

320
00:16:26.240 --> 00:16:27.520
Ten years older.

321
00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:28.920
Yeah.

322
00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:30.040
Right.

323
00:16:30.120 --> 00:16:31.160
Me,

324
00:16:31.960 --> 00:16:33.880
ten years older...

325
00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:36.720
I am older.

326
00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:39.320
I'm an old man.

327
00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:42.880
I'm a lonely old man.

328
00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:44.480
No, you're not.

329
00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:46.880
There's not a single soul around me.

330
00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:51.280
I'm sitting on a bench all alone.

331
00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:53.720
There are branches.

332
00:16:54.440 --> 00:16:56.840
The wind is blowing,
the sun is shining,

333
00:16:56.880 --> 00:16:59.960
but I'm sitting there alone
with my watery eyes and wrinkles.

334
00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:04.160
You can't be all alone,
you'll have the kids.

335
00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:06.280
Yeah...

336
00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:09.320
Try it yourself.
Let's see what's going on with you.

337
00:17:11.120 --> 00:17:12.200
So...

338
00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:15.480
Ten years later.

339
00:17:18.920 --> 00:17:21.200
Oh God!
- What?

340
00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:24.960
I'm a grandma.
- Maybe it's Ave?

341
00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:27.200
Or Mihkel?
- Good point.

342
00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:29.680
Try it again,
but this time properly.

343
00:17:29.720 --> 00:17:31.160
Alright, I'll try.

344
00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:32.960
Okay...

345
00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:35.400
Me...

346
00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:39.480
I'm still alone on the bench.
- Are you doing this on purpose?

347
00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:41.760
I'm not.
- Focus properly.

348
00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:42.840
I'm focusing.

349
00:17:43.720 --> 00:17:45.880
I can see it, I'm alone.

350
00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:47.880
No, I'm a grandpa.

351
00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:50.840
But I'm a lonely grandpa.

352
00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:54.120
I'm a lonely grandpa.

353
00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:57.080
Are you at least content?

354
00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:00.680
Are you happy?

355
00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:03.400
Are you?

356
00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:09.160
I was smiling in my vision.

357
00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:11.160
I'm happy for you.

358
00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:15.400
Aksel.

359
00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:20.400
You know what?

360
00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:24.240
I have to actually figure out
who I'll be in ten minutes.

361
00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:28.360
When everything has been
taken from me - the job, the house.

362
00:18:30.680 --> 00:18:32.800
God, ten years.

363
00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:35.400
That's eons away.

364
00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:44.200
So, you came to see the house?

365
00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:46.800
Laura, my wife, did mention

366
00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:49.080
that the relator
called about your visit.

367
00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:51.520
I'll show you...
Just step right here.

368
00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:57.040
Can you feel a cold breath here?

369
00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:00.720
Around the shins?

370
00:19:00.880 --> 00:19:04.880
Like a piercing cold wind?
A cold breath?

371
00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:09.880
The thing is, this house
is built on top of an old cemetery.

372
00:19:09.880 --> 00:19:12.560
There's some kind of an energy here.

373
00:19:12.600 --> 00:19:14.160
It's kind of funny.

374
00:19:14.360 --> 00:19:17.280
Unless you want to sleep at night.

375
00:19:17.320 --> 00:19:21.880
The wind is trying to communicate,
it wants to say something.

376
00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:23.560
Your legs start to hurt.

377
00:19:23.920 --> 00:19:27.480
It whines and
whistles through the night.

378
00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:32.120
Some spirits want to...

379
00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:35.120
Hello.
Sorry, I'm a little late.

380
00:19:35.160 --> 00:19:36.640
You made it.

381
00:19:36.680 --> 00:19:40.200
We already talked
about the wind, honey.

382
00:19:41.920 --> 00:19:44.480
Thank you for coming.

383
00:19:51.200 --> 00:19:52.880
What did you tell her?

384
00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:53.920
Nothing.

385
00:19:54.720 --> 00:19:57.800
I was just telling her about
the cosy spirit of our home.

386
00:19:58.040 --> 00:20:01.040
You fooling around
and being weird won't help.

387
00:20:01.360 --> 00:20:03.400
You're making things worse.

388
00:20:09.880 --> 00:20:11.120
Stop it.

389
00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:28.600
Tauno.

390
00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:36.720
Hey, have a look at this.

391
00:20:36.720 --> 00:20:39.840
Hunting hats for babies.
Isn't this cute?

392
00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:42.760
They have it in green, too.
- Tauno...

393
00:20:43.440 --> 00:20:44.960
Tauno.
- Mirjam.

394
00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:46.560
Wait.

395
00:20:47.320 --> 00:20:50.480
We need to keep the temple clean.

396
00:20:50.920 --> 00:20:52.280
That's it.

397
00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:54.400
Everything that may upset the baby.

398
00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:57.080
Sex and alcohol.

399
00:20:58.080 --> 00:21:01.040
Abrupt moves and
bad moods are in the past.

400
00:21:01.080 --> 00:21:02.920
Am I an incubator to you?

401
00:21:02.920 --> 00:21:05.520
Mirjam, it's all for the baby.

402
00:21:05.560 --> 00:21:07.240
What am I then?

403
00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:09.600
Is everything alright?

404
00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:10.720
Is it?

405
00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:12.000
Is it?

406
00:21:12.280 --> 00:21:14.320
Is it?

407
00:21:17.520 --> 00:21:19.120
We're having a baby.

408
00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:20.800
That's most important.

409
00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:24.920
Get this.

410
00:21:25.480 --> 00:21:29.320
Rihard sent these to
the bakery with a dinner invitation.

411
00:21:29.400 --> 00:21:32.080
Wow, you're...

412
00:21:33.120 --> 00:21:35.360
...serious about this millionaire.

413
00:21:35.400 --> 00:21:38.040
Will you go on the date?
- I don't know.

414
00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:39.880
He just...

415
00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:42.800
He makes me feel special.

416
00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:44.960
Asks me for advice.

417
00:21:45.640 --> 00:21:48.320
I feel like someone's
interested in me.

418
00:21:49.080 --> 00:21:51.480
That someone's
interested in my ideas.

419
00:21:52.280 --> 00:21:53.600
What will you do?

420
00:21:53.840 --> 00:21:56.120
I think I'll accept the invitation.

421
00:21:56.160 --> 00:21:58.280
It doesn't oblige me to anything.

422
00:21:58.320 --> 00:22:01.160
Of course.
It's the opposite for me.

423
00:22:01.240 --> 00:22:02.640
What?

424
00:22:04.400 --> 00:22:05.400
Well...

425
00:22:06.640 --> 00:22:09.360
Tauno's pregnant in his head.
He's like...

426
00:22:09.560 --> 00:22:12.080
...a big curly headed boob.

427
00:22:12.600 --> 00:22:16.320
He doesn't notice me at all.
I'm just a package for this child.

428
00:22:16.360 --> 00:22:17.720
Stop it.

429
00:22:17.760 --> 00:22:19.880
It's true.
I should conduct an experiment.

430
00:22:19.920 --> 00:22:22.200
What experiment?
- I don't know.

431
00:22:22.200 --> 00:22:24.240
See if he even cares
about me anymore.

432
00:22:25.520 --> 00:22:27.960
Is it possible?
A hunter, pregnant in his head?

433
00:22:27.960 --> 00:22:29.600
Mirjam, cut it out.

434
00:22:29.640 --> 00:22:31.880
You're just a bit stressed.

435
00:22:31.880 --> 00:22:33.960
Do you know what makes you stressed?

436
00:22:34.200 --> 00:22:37.200
Somebody saying
that you're a bit stressed.

437
00:22:37.560 --> 00:22:38.560
Sorry.

438
00:22:41.080 --> 00:22:42.080
Okay.

439
00:22:42.400 --> 00:22:45.960
Yes, I'm stressed.
I'm going home.

440
00:22:46.240 --> 00:22:48.280
Meditate a bit.
- Of course.

441
00:22:48.320 --> 00:22:50.920
It's a difficult time right now.

442
00:22:50.920 --> 00:22:53.240
It'll get better soon.

443
00:22:53.280 --> 00:22:55.040
You keep telling me that yourself.

444
00:23:13.760 --> 00:23:14.840
So...

445
00:23:16.920 --> 00:23:18.800
The divorce agreement.

446
00:23:19.800 --> 00:23:21.680
We'll put our signatures here

447
00:23:21.680 --> 00:23:24.600
and then take it to
the vital statistics office.

448
00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:30.960
You fooling around and
being weird won't change anything.

449
00:23:31.560 --> 00:23:32.840
I'm just sorry.

450
00:23:33.520 --> 00:23:36.280
That all this therapy didn't help.

451
00:23:36.400 --> 00:23:37.640
It did help.

452
00:23:38.280 --> 00:23:40.080
Really well.

453
00:23:41.240 --> 00:23:44.360
It's really helping
this divorce, just...

454
00:23:46.040 --> 00:23:47.800
It's helping in the wrong way.

455
00:23:48.840 --> 00:23:50.760
It's helping in the
opposite direction.

456
00:23:53.480 --> 00:23:55.200
So you've decided?

457
00:23:56.400 --> 00:23:58.480
Those flowers in the kitchen.

458
00:23:58.720 --> 00:24:02.240
That doesn't mean anything yet.

459
00:24:05.280 --> 00:24:06.800
Okay.

460
00:24:09.320 --> 00:24:11.680
The paper is sacred.

461
00:24:21.120 --> 00:24:22.240
Okay.

462
00:24:23.120 --> 00:24:25.160
Now, the joint application
for divorce.

463
00:24:25.200 --> 00:24:28.920
We have to take it to
the vital statistics office together.

464
00:24:28.920 --> 00:24:30.080
Alright, together.

465
00:24:31.800 --> 00:24:34.640
I already filled out your fields.

466
00:24:43.520 --> 00:24:45.280
All of this is unreal.

467
00:24:49.720 --> 00:24:51.560
All those years here.

468
00:24:53.080 --> 00:24:54.560
Our university years.

469
00:24:56.440 --> 00:24:59.440
Those years in the beginning,
when we lived in that bunker.

470
00:25:00.080 --> 00:25:01.520
God...

471
00:25:01.880 --> 00:25:03.800
It won't go anywhere.

472
00:25:04.640 --> 00:25:06.640
We'll carry it with us.

473
00:25:08.640 --> 00:25:11.680
A divorce doesn't
wipe out the memories.

474
00:25:13.760 --> 00:25:15.120
Sadly not.

475
00:25:31.880 --> 00:25:33.840
Aksel, stay away.

476
00:25:33.840 --> 00:25:36.040
We have to sell the house.

477
00:25:36.080 --> 00:25:37.920
Calm down, I'll sell it.

478
00:25:42.120 --> 00:25:44.040
Hello.
- Hello.

479
00:25:44.120 --> 00:25:45.800
Did you come to see the house?
- Yes.

480
00:25:45.840 --> 00:25:47.480
Step right in.

481
00:25:47.520 --> 00:25:49.320
We'll show it to you.

482
00:25:49.440 --> 00:25:51.240
This is my wife.
- Hello.

483
00:25:51.240 --> 00:25:52.240
Hello.

484
00:25:53.080 --> 00:25:54.200
Hello.

485
00:25:54.920 --> 00:25:57.840
So, this is the living room.

486
00:25:58.560 --> 00:26:01.760
This has life in many ways.

487
00:26:02.200 --> 00:26:03.520
It's the heart of the house.

488
00:26:03.560 --> 00:26:06.320
The most important place
for family gatherings.

489
00:26:06.360 --> 00:26:08.360
The place for important
family meetings.

490
00:26:08.360 --> 00:26:11.760
This is the field of
democracy for families.

491
00:26:11.800 --> 00:26:15.480
The birth place of
good and important decisions.

492
00:26:16.080 --> 00:26:19.880
I'll show you the bedroom upstairs.
The master bedroom.

493
00:26:20.240 --> 00:26:23.240
The crown jewel
of fondness and harmony.

494
00:26:23.880 --> 00:26:25.960
Yeah, I...

495
00:26:26.400 --> 00:26:30.120
I feel so happy in this house.
If I wasn't moving out,

496
00:26:30.240 --> 00:26:32.280
I wouldn't even leave.

497
00:26:32.320 --> 00:26:36.280
I wouldn't even go to the shop.
We've spent many good days here.

498
00:26:36.800 --> 00:26:39.200
Yeah, it's...

499
00:26:39.880 --> 00:26:45.320
Can you feel how the walls
have retained all of the happiness?

500
00:26:45.640 --> 00:26:49.960
It's a house where any normal family
will become absurdly happy.

501
00:26:51.280 --> 00:26:52.720
Can you feel it?

502
00:26:52.760 --> 00:26:54.800
The aura of happiness here?

503
00:26:56.320 --> 00:26:58.080
That there is the kitchen.

504
00:26:58.560 --> 00:27:00.920
This kitchen is quite special.

505
00:27:00.960 --> 00:27:03.480
Wonderful.
Let's be in touch then.

506
00:27:07.640 --> 00:27:11.480
They will schedule an appointment
at the notary and then it's a go.

507
00:27:11.920 --> 00:27:13.640
They didn't even try to bargain.

508
00:27:14.720 --> 00:27:17.120
You have skills as a salesman.

509
00:27:17.800 --> 00:27:19.880
My heart bled empty.

510
00:27:20.080 --> 00:27:22.240
Then you're ready to be a salesman.

511
00:27:22.400 --> 00:27:24.640
Salesmen don't have
blood in their hearts.

512
00:27:24.720 --> 00:27:26.400
Only the sound of coins.

513
00:27:26.800 --> 00:27:30.080
Thank you for the enthusiasm.
I guess I'll consider it.

514
00:27:34.800 --> 00:27:36.320
Thank you, Aksel.

515
00:27:37.480 --> 00:27:38.760
You're welcome.

516
00:28:16.760 --> 00:28:17.760
Sorry.

517
00:28:17.760 --> 00:28:19.320
No, listen on.

518
00:28:21.000 --> 00:28:22.240
But you don't like it.

519
00:28:24.320 --> 00:28:25.480
Funny.

520
00:28:25.960 --> 00:28:29.200
After all these years
I think I'm starting to.

521
00:28:30.720 --> 00:28:31.720
Really?

522
00:28:35.880 --> 00:28:38.760
I can't get that image
out of my head.

523
00:28:39.480 --> 00:28:42.080
Your vision in ten years' time.

524
00:28:42.960 --> 00:28:45.640
A lonely old man under a tree.

525
00:28:48.480 --> 00:28:50.680
You'll have your music.

526
00:28:52.000 --> 00:28:53.880
It'll still bring joy, right?

527
00:29:14.360 --> 00:29:15.360
I've had enough.

528
00:29:16.240 --> 00:29:19.240
I left.
It's the only test I know how to do.

529
00:29:19.320 --> 00:29:21.360
Mirjam, what...?

530
00:29:24.640 --> 00:29:26.280
What did Tauno do?

531
00:29:26.480 --> 00:29:28.920
That's the thing.
He didn't do anything.
